# The rendered page is compared byte for byte: `cs-ledger check` re-renders the
# records and asserts the committed ledger.html matches. A checkout on Windows
# applies core.autocrlf, rewrites the page to CRLF, and the freshness gate then
# fails for a reason no diff explains.
#
# The scripts here carry a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang, which the same rewrite
# turns into `bash\r` — an error naming the interpreter rather than the script.
#
# text=auto still lets git detect and leave binaries alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
